// @test: typecheck-pass
// @tier: 0
// @level: L1
// @tags: rank2, generics, archive, T0997
// @timeout: 60000
// @description: Two DIFFERENT instantiations of a rank-2 method in one file each get their own quantified variable
//
// LEVEL. Filed under L3-extended because "rank-2" and "dependent types"
// sound experimental. The DEFECT is not: a second call site silently
// inherited the first one's element type, so a program got the wrong
// type and the mismatch was reported at the wrong place. That is
// "type system, inference" — L1-core — and it matters because only
// L0 and L1 gate a merge. A pin for a soundness hole that does not
// gate is a pin that records the fix rather than protecting it.

// A rank-2 function type — `fn<R>(Reducer<B, R>) -> Reducer<A, R>` —
// promises that R is chosen by the CALLEE, for every R. Two call sites
// with different element types must therefore be independent.
//
// Measured before the repair: the second function reported
//
//     error<E400>: Type mismatch: expected 'Int', found 'Text'
//
// where `Int` is the element type of the FIRST function. The order of
// CALLS does not matter; the order of DECLARATIONS does.
//
// ROOT. The quantifier does not survive the stdlib bake. The rank-2
// type reference renders as `__opaque_typeref`, because its
// spelling `fn<N>(…)` carries a COUNT rather than names and so has
// nothing for `parse_descriptor_type_string` to bind. The archive
// therefore stores one instantiation per entry — `Reducer<A, Int>` —
// and the second call site is handed the first one's answer.
//
// The decision was documented WITH its condition, at
// `archive_metadata.rs`: "Zero occurrences in the shipped archive, so
// the placeholder costs nothing today; giving it a real spelling is a
// parser-side change first." The condition expired when `Transducer`
// and `StatefulTransducer` were added — four rank-2 fields now ship in
// `core/base/iterator.vr`.
//
// `only_text` is the CONTROL and is deliberately first: one
// instantiation always passed, so a repair that breaks rank-2 handling
// outright fails there before reaching the two-instantiation case.

mount core.base.iterator.{StatefulTransducer, Transducer};

fn only_text() {
    let xform: StatefulTransducer<Text, (Int, Text), Int> = Transducer.enumerate();
    let data = ["a", "b", "c"];
    let r: List<(Int, Text)> = data.iter().map(|x| *x).transduce_stateful(xform).collect();
}

fn first_int() {
    let data = [1, 1, 2];
    let xform: StatefulTransducer<Int, Int, Maybe<Int>> = Transducer.dedupe();
    let r: List<Int> = data.iter().map(|x| *x).transduce_stateful(xform).collect();
}

fn then_text() {
    let xform: StatefulTransducer<Text, (Int, Text), Int> = Transducer.enumerate();
    let data = ["a", "b", "c"];
    let r: List<(Int, Text)> = data.iter().map(|x| *x).transduce_stateful(xform).collect();
}

fn main() {
    print("rank-2 survives two instantiations");
}
